<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila firm invites Petronas for naphtha plant.</title>
<headline>Manila firm invites Petronas for naphtha plant.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Petrochemicals Corp of Asia Pacific (Petrocorp) said on Tuesday it has invited Petroliam Nasional Berhad (Petronas) of Malaysia to participate in a consortium to build a naphtha cracker plant.</p>
<p>Petrocorp chairman Antonio Garcia told a news conference on Tuesday he had asked the Malaysian national oil company about participation in the consortium planning to build the 500,000 tonnes-a-year naphtha plant.</p>
<p>Petronas is yet to decide on the offer, he said.</p>
<p>Petrocorp is a consortium composed of Chemical Industries of the Philippines (Chemphil), Basic Petroleum &amp; Minerals Inc, Thai Petrochemical Industry Plc, local firms All Asia Capital and Agatha Builders.</p>
<p>- Manila newsroom 63 2 8418936 fax 8176267</p>
</text>
